          "explanation": "The question asks whether anyone staffs the statistics help desk on Wednesday evenings, so a good answer has to confirm or deny that staffing and, ideally, say something about who and when. \"Yes, two tutors are there Wednesdays until about nine\" does exactly that: it confirms that the desk is covered, names who covers it, and adds the closing time, which is precisely the kind of detail the speaker needs. The reply \"No, I've never taken a statistics course here myself\" answers a question that was never asked; the speaker wanted to know about the help desk's hours, not about the responder's personal coursework, so it shifts to an irrelevant topic. \"Sure, the evening lecture usually ends around eight thirty\" reacts to the word \"evening\" rather than to the meaning of the question; lecture times say nothing about whether tutors are staffing a help desk. Finally, \"Right, the desk was completely removed from campus last year\" is impossible given what the speaker just said, because it begins by agreeing and then claims the desk no longer exists, which contradicts the premise of a question about who is working there this Wednesday.",
